{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Let me cross over</b> the Jordan — 50 amot. Do not cross over, but one amah:" "<b>and the Lebanon</b> defective vav, on account of six things that are in this Torah: for olah, for minhah, for chatat, for asham, for millu'im, and for zevach shelamim. From ואתחנן until והלבנון — 40 words, to say: remember for me the 40 days I stood before You on the mountain. A person should always arrange the praise of the Place and afterward pray — from where do we learn it? From Moses:" "<b>Your greatness</b> — this is the great El. <b>Your strong hand</b> — this is You, mighty. <b>Who is El in heaven</b> — corresponding to <b>You are holy</b>. <b>Let me cross over</b>. A person should not ask his needs in the first three:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:41.463427770Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}